course: dictionary
lesson: 9713
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning. The context, meaning the words and sentences around it, tells you which meaning is right. Take «sum». It can be a maths answer, a maths problem, an amount of money, or a way of saying the main points.
explain: In maths, the sum is the answer you get when you add numbers. The sum of 3 and 4 is 7. In the UK, a sum is also a maths problem, as in «do your sums». When a sentence says «the sum of two numbers is 20», the word sum is a strong clue that you need to add.
explain: Outside maths, a sum of money is an amount of money. «A large sum» means a lot of money. In writing, «to sum up» means to say the main points briefly, and «in sum» means the same thing. Ask yourself: is this about numbers, money, or telling the main points?
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: The sum of 3 and 4 is 7, so the word sum means the answer when you add.
fact: «Do the sum» means work out the calculation, as in «always do the sum» when comparing prices.
fact: «To sum up» means to say the main points briefly.
fact: Sum can be a noun or a verb: sums, summed, summing.
exercise: What does sum mean in «the sum of 3 and 4»? | A piece of writing | *The answer you get when you add | A lump of money | A take-away, the answer you get when you subtract
exercise: Ella says «do your sums» means sing a song. What does it really mean? | *Do your maths problems | Count the sweets | Write a story | Sing a song
exercise: Mia says, «In sum, the plan worked.» What does in sum mean here? | A loud noise | A question about numbers | A large amount of money | *Briefly, the main points are these
test: «The biggest pack is often cheaper per unit, but not always, so always do the sum.» What does do the sum mean here? | *Work out which pack costs less | Count the packs in the shop | Eat the biggest pack | Sing the price
test: The sum of two numbers is 20 and one number is 8. What is the missing number? | 28 | 8 | *12 | 160
exam: Which sentence uses sum to mean an amount of money? | Do your sums before bed | *She saved a large sum for her trip | To sum up, the story ends happily | The sum of 5 and 6 is 11
